        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-10T12:58:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Makes sense to me, I\u0027ll update the corresponding HVC handler in CrosVM once we\u0027ve decided on an ABI. Note that this will need to be manually cherry-picked into Android, as they\u0027ve stopped the regular merges until the release, AFAIU. So the earlier we make the change, the better!",
      "parentUuid": "75bd3d56_db6aaa8c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 566,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 566,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "32163a35cbeb3b364c5d2e87cb3437c47db2f8b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90808a95_f8cc6730",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/device/device.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 566,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-10T13:15:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can say IPA is an arg for the function (now PWR_ON/PWR_OFF)\n\nbut I am convinced the right way for DVFS is just to transmit a value of utilisation to the host. Just like it says power on/off for a specific device, it would send an utilisation for that very same device and then the host does what it has to do with it.\n\nThis is similar to the scheduling hint with uclamp we send. This is just an utilisation between 0 and 1024. No need to know the CPU OPP or even the topology. I don\u0027t see any reason why devfreq should be different",
      "parentUuid": "2f10ec99_436d98e5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 566,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 566,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "32163a35cbeb3b364c5d2e87cb3437c47db2f8b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b4a09343_ece7145f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/device/device.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 566,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-10T13:19:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I don\u0027t see any reason why devfreq should be different\n\nOne aspect worth mentioning (although I believe I agree with you overall) is the fact that it will most likely be the same driver running on both the host and guest so such abstraction would mean that vendors need to maintain 2 sets of OPP (physical \u0026 abstract/virtual) but I\u0027m not sure how much of an issue that is.\n\nIt might actually be better in case host \u0026 guests need the different tables because the respective underlying mechanisms for OPP transitions have different latencies...?",
      "parentUuid": "90808a95_f8cc6730",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 566,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 566,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "32163a35cbeb3b364c5d2e87cb3437c47db2f8b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
